  "details": "- CVE-2026-87910: tarfile: skip a link member when the extraction filter\n  returns None for its hardlink-extraction fallback instead of ignoring the\n  filter result\n- CVE-2026-17084: stringprep: build the RFC 3454 B.2/B.3 tables from Unicode\n  3.2.0 data so IDNA 2003 encoding of newly case-folding characters no longer\n  depends on the interpreter's Unicode version\n- CVE-2026-15310: zipfile: bound the output of each bzip2/LZMA decompress()\n  call so a small crafted member cannot trigger an unbounded allocation\n- CVE-2026-9669: bz2: refuse to reuse a BZ2Decompressor after a decompression\n  error, so retrying with the same object can no longer resume from an invalid\n  internal state and write out of bounds",
